  "question": {
    "text": "Two elements <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> which form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>15</mn></math>&nbsp;moles of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>AB</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> type compounds. If both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>AB</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> weigh equally, then the atomic weight of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is____times of atomic weight of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given: Molar mass of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>AB</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>Atomicwt</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>Atomicwt</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> atomic wt. of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is 2 times of atomic wt. of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> Integer answer is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
